        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate core case attributes"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773822846989"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_CORE_CASE_ATTRIBUTES",
          "id": "1770110724199",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770110724201_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Role\nYou are a Case Management Specialist. Your goal is to analyze an incoming user query and convert it into a structured case with professional titles, objective descriptions, and accurate classifications.\n\n# Input Data\n- `User Query`: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n-  `Grievance Contributing Factors` : {{$context.$nodes?.GET_CLEANEDUP_GRIEVANCE_CONTRIBUTING_FACTORS?.$output?.result}} \n- `DA Contributing Factors` : {{$context.$nodes?.GET_CLEANEDUP_DA_CONTRIBUTING_FACTORS?.$output?.result}} \n- `Stripe Code` : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.StripeCd}} \n\n# Classification Criteria & Mapping\n- Evaluate the `User Query` and determine the **Case Type** based strictly on the presence of these **Contributing Factors**:\n\n### 1. GRIEVANCE\n- Analyze `User Query` and compare the the contributing factors of the incident with the \"Meaning\" field of `Grievance Contributing Factors`. **Only** if relevant match is found then return \"caseType\" as \"GRIEVANCE\" and return the list of multiple relevant contributing factors as \"contributingFactors\".\n- Exclusions: Ignore meanings titled \"Not Applicable\".\n\n### 2. DISCIPLINARY ACTIONS\n- Analyze `User Query` and compare the the contributing factors of the incident with the \"Meaning\" field of `DA Contributing Factors`. **Only** if relevant match is found then return \"caseType\" as \"DISCIPLINARY ACTIONS\" and return the list of multiple relevant contributing factors as \"contributingFactors\". \n- Exclusions: Ignore meanings titled \"Unknown\" or \"Unspecified\".\n\n### 3. NONE\n- Assign if the `User Query` does not clearly match any **Contributing Factors** listed above.\n\n# Stripe Code Classification Criteria & Mapping\n- Evaluate the `Stripe Code` provided in input. If its value is either \"ORA_SVC_CRM\", \"ORA_SVC_HRHD\" or \"ORA_SVC_ISR\" , then return it as stripeCd in the output. Otherwise, follow the following steps :\n\n### 1. CRM (Customer Relationship Management)\n- Select this if the `User Query` is driven by an interaction with an external party. It is valid when the primary goal is managing the lifecycle of a customer, tracking their specific service history, or resolving a client-facing ticket to maintain a healthy business-to-customer relationship.\n- Return ORA_SVC_CRM as stripeCd in the output. \n\n### 2. HRHD (HR Help Desk)\n- Select this if the `User Query` is employee-centric regarding their life at the company. It is valid for \"Individual-to-Company\" matters such as personal wellness, pay/benefit disputes, time-off requests, or sensitive interpersonal issues like conduct, grievances or disciplinary actions.\n- Return ORA_SVC_HRHD as stripeCd in the output. \n\n### 3. ISR (Internal Service Request)\n- Select this if the `User Query` is task-centric or operational. It is valid when an employee is seeking the functional \"means\" to do their job, such as requesting a workspace fix, troubleshooting tech equipment, or asking for support from internal departments like Finance or Sales Ops.\n- Return ORA_SVC_ISR as stripeCd in the output. \n\n\n# Instructions\n1. **caseTitle**: Create a concise, relevant and professional title with brief info of the case (max 10 words and within 400 characters).\n2. **caseDescription**: Write a clear, factual summary of the user's issue. Maintain an objective tone (max 1000 characters).\n3. **caseType**: Select exactly one from: `GRIEVANCE`, `DISCIPLINARY ACTIONS`, or `NONE`.\n4. **contributingFactors**: \n   - If `caseType` is **GRIEVANCE** or **DISCIPLINARY ACTIONS**, return a single string of Lookup Codes separated only by commas (e.g., \"ORA_SVC_THEFT,ORA_SVC_LATE_FOR_WORK\").\n   - If `caseType` is **NONE**, return an empty string \"\".\n5. **Constraint**: Output ONLY a valid JSON object.\n\n# Output Format\n```json\n{\n  \"caseTitle\": \"string\",\n  \"caseDescription\": \"string\",\n  \"stripeCd\": \"string\",\n  \"caseType\": \"GRIEVANCE | DISCIPLINARY ACTIONS | NONE\",\n  \"contributingFactors\": \"string\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"caseTitle\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"caseDescription\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"stripeCd\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"caseType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"contributingFactors\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1771587077624",
            "name": "Switch to relevant case type"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "DISCIPLINARY ACTIONS": "1771449272116",
            "NONE": "1771587077624",
            "GRIEVANCE": "1771449619635"
          },
          "code": "SWITCH_TO_RELEVANT_CASE_TYPE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770110962493",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770110962495_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_CORE_CASE_ATTRIBUTES.$output.caseType}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set DA related fields"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771587209211"
          },
          "code": "SET_DA_RELATED_FIELDS",
          "id": "1771323010145",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771323010149_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Role\nYou are a Case Specialist. Your goal is to analyze a user query and map it to specific Measures Taken, Reviewer and occurrence date for a Disciplinary Action Case.\n\n# Input Data\n- **User Query**: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- **Measures Taken Reference**: {{$context.$nodes?.CLEANEDUP_MEASURES_TAKEN?.$output?.result}} \n- **Reviewed by Reference**: {{$context.$nodes?.CLEANEDUP_REVIEWED_BY?.$output?.result}} \n- **Current System Date**: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} \n\n# Instructions\n1. **Incident Occurrence Date**: \n   - Extract the date the incident happened from the `User Query`.\n   - If a specific date is found, convert it to this exact format: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss+00:00`.\n   - If no date is mentioned, use the **Current System Date** in the exact format: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss+00:00`.\n\n2. **Measures taken**:\n   - Analyze `User Query` for any actions, interventions, or steps already implemented in response to the incident. \n   - Search the 'Meaning' field in `Measures Taken Reference` for a direct or semantic match to the actions found in previous point. \n   - **Only** if relevant matches are found, return a string of comma separated 'LookupCode' for all the relevant measures taken.\n \n3. **Reviewed By**:\n   - Analyze `User Query` and look for the reviewed by details. Like any mentions of individuals, departments, or authorities who have already examined or \"signed off\" on the event.\n   - Search the 'Meaning' field in `Reviewed by Reference` for a direct or semantic match to the reviewed by details found in previous point. \n   - **Only** if relevant matches are found, return a string of comma separated 'LookupCode' for all the relevant reviewed by meanings.\n\n# Output Format\n```json\n{\n  \"incidentOccurrenceDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss+00:00\",\n  \"measuresTaken\": \"string\",\n  \"reviewedBy\": \"string\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"reviewedBy\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"measuresTaken\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"incidentOccurrenceDate\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set grievance related fields"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771499253267"
          },
          "code": "SET_GRIEVANCE_RELATED_FIELDS",
          "id": "1771323035074",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771323035076_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Role\nYou are a Case Specialist. Your goal is to analyze a user query and map it to specific Incident Type, Allegation and occurrence date for a Grievance Case.\n\n# Input Data\n- **User Query**: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n- **Incident Type Reference**: {{$context.$nodes?.CLEANEDUP_INCIDENT_DATA?.$output?.result}} \n- **Allegation Reference**: {{$context.$nodes?.CLEANEDUP_ALLEGATIONS_DATA?.$output?.result}} \n- **Current System Date**: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} \n\n# Instructions\n1. **Incident Occurrence Date**: \n   - Extract the date the incident happened from the `User Query`.\n   - If a specific date is found, convert it to this exact format: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss+00:00`.\n   - If no date is mentioned, use the **Current System Date** in the exact format: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss+00:00`.\n\n2. **Incident Type**:\n   - Analyze `User Query` and look for the part where the type of incident or event is mentioned. \n   - Search the 'Meaning' field in `Incident Type Reference` for a direct or semantic match to the event found in previous point. (e.g., \"Operational Change\", \"Remote Work\", \"Work Environment\").\n   - **Only** if relevant match is found, return the corresponding 'LookupCode' for the most relevant incident type. \n\n3. **Allegation**:\n   - Analyze the \"Who/How\" (the accusation or tone of the grievance) in the `User Query`.\n   - Search the 'Meaning' field in `Allegation Reference` for a direct or semantic match to the allegation found in previous point. \n   - **Only** if relevant match is found, return the corresponding 'LookupCode' for the most relevant allegation.\n\n# Output Format\n```json\n{\n  \"incidentOccurrenceDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss+00:00\",\n  \"incidentType\": \"string\",\n  \"allegation\": \"string\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"incidentOccurrenceDate\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"incidentType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"allegation\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
